  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "zend_add_helper_SPEC",
    "file": "php-src/Zend/zend_vm_execute.h",
    "description": "The root cause is that zend_add_helper_SPEC forwards op_1/op_2 directly to add_function() after only checking for IS_UNDEF, but does not validate that the zval pointers themselves are valid/live VM operands. Under this PoV\u2019s corrupted execution state, one ADD operand pointer is wild, and add_function_fast() immediately dereferences it via Z_TYPE_P(op1)/zval_get_type(), causing an invalid read SEGV. So the bug is unsafe operand-state propagation in the VM helper, not arithmetic logic in add_function_fast itself.",
    "conditions": "Trigger requires malformed script/JIT tracing state that leads the ADD opcode handler (ZEND_ADD_SPEC_TMPVARCV_TMPVARCV_HANDLER -> zend_add_helper_SPEC) to receive an invalid operand zval pointer (not merely UNDEF type). The helper passes this unchecked pointer into add_function(); add_function_fast then reads op type bytes (TYPE_PAIR(Z_TYPE_P(op1), Z_TYPE_P(op2))) and crashes on the wild address. Data flow: fuzzed PHP source -> compilation/JIT trace generation with corrupted state -> VM ADD handler gets poisoned operand pointer -> unchecked dereference in arithmetic fast path."
  },
